<title>USA: Denver Airport $280 mln bonds repriced, ylds cut.</title>
<headline>Denver Airport $280 mln bonds repriced, ylds cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said Tuesday it repriced Denver, Colo.'s $280 million airport system revenue bond deal, lowering yields in several maturities and cutting the top yield in 2013 to 5.85 percent from 5.90 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>CITY AND COUNTY OF DENVER, COLORADO</p>
<p>RE: $279,570,000*</p>
<p>for and on behalf of its Department of Aviation</p>
<p>Verbal award.</p>
<p>The account is closed.</p>
